# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in the FZ key, then the tools in tools/ can
# decrypt the ASUS .FZ schematic export. The `.env` file is gitignored - the key
# is never committed.
#
# OBV_FZKEY is the 44-word RC6 key that OpenBoardView uses to decrypt ASUS
# .FZ boardview files. Give it as 44 comma- or space-separated 0x hex words.
#
# Where to get it:
#   The key is the standard, publicly-circulated OpenBoardView FZ key. It is NOT
#   generated per-board and is not secret to this project - it validates against
#   the parity signature built into OpenBoardView (FZFile::getKeyParity()).
#   Obtain it from any of:
#     1. Your own OpenBoardView config after you have entered it once:
#          ~/.config/OpenBoardView/obv.conf   (Linux)
#          %APPDATA%/OpenBoardView/obv.conf   (Windows)
#        Copy the 44 values from the `FZKey = ...` line.
#     2. Community OpenBoardView `obv.conf` files shared online. Search the web
#        for:  OpenBoardView  FZKey  obv.conf
#        (e.g. boardview/repair forums and pastebins that publish a full
#        44-value `FZKey = 0x..., 0x..., ...` line).
#   Verify you have all 44 words: a 36-word copy that circulates will fail the
#   parity check. extract_fz.py checks the count and errors out if it is wrong.
#
OBV_FZKEY=0x00000000, 0x00000000, 0x00000000, 0x00000000, 0x00000000, 0x00000000, 0x00000000, 0x00000000, 0x00000000, 0x00000000, 0x00000000, 0x00000000, 0x00000000, 0x00000000, 0x00000000, 0x00000000, 0x00000000, 0x00000000, 0x00000000, 0x00000000, 0x00000000, 0x00000000, 0x00000000, 0x00000000, 0x00000000, 0x00000000, 0x00000000, 0x00000000, 0x00000000, 0x00000000, 0x00000000, 0x00000000, 0x00000000, 0x00000000, 0x00000000, 0x00000000, 0x00000000, 0x00000000, 0x00000000, 0x00000000, 0x00000000, 0x00000000, 0x00000000, 0x00000000
